{"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"MatomoEncoding","modules":[{"name":"MatomoEncoding"}],"externalID":"MatomoEncoding","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Matomo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Matomo"},{"title":"Custom dimensions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoUnmappedProperty"],"anchor":"Custom-dimensions"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/matomoencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") for one site of a Matomo installation in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one call. It checks the installation’s URL, the site ID, the category and the custom dimensions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then posts bulk tracking requests to the installation’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Each batch is split to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": 20 records a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request, as Matomo’s iOS SDK sends them, and 1,000,000 bytes a request, under the 1 MiB that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nginx takes in a body by default, as Matomo documents no limit. A batch with no record the encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out, so import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo takes events from anyone who can reach it, so the destination needs no key, and builds on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every platform: an app sends to Matomo directly.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MatomoEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let matomo = try HTTPDestination.matomo(","    url: url,  \/\/ where Matomo is installed: https:\/\/analytics.example.com","    siteID: 3,  \/\/ the app's site in Matomo","    dimensions: [\"plan\": 1],  \/\/ custom dimensions made in Matomo","    category: \"Shop\",  \/\/ each event's category","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: matomo)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"url","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is where Matomo is installed, with its path if it has one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/example.com\/matomo\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), not the tracker’s endpoint: the destination appends ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError","isActive":true},{"text":" for a URL that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", has no host, holds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user name, password, query or fragment, or already ends in a ","type":"text"},{"code":".php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"matomo.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a site ID below 1; for a category that is empty once trimmed, or longer than the 4,096 characters","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo stores; and for dimensions that break a rule, listed below.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"No token_auth","anchor":"No-tokenauth"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination sends no ","type":"text"},{"code":"token_auth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and takes none. A token is a secret, and anything an app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ships can be read out of it, so a token in an app gives anyone who has the app the token’s rights","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over your Matomo.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without a token, Matomo takes an event’s time (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cdt"},{"text":") only when it is less than a day old, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses one more than a day ahead. It answers 200 to such a request all the same, and stores","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing, so the encoder leaves out every record tracked more than 23 hours before or after it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encodes the batch, and the destination reports it, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that disagree. So a record that waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"more than 23 hours to be encoded, kept by a store through a long time offline or waiting in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer behind a failing delivery, is reported as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and never reaches Matomo.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request is encoded once, and each retry sends the same bytes, so the encoder gives each request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A request still failing by then isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent again, as it would reach Matomo too late to be stored: the destination drops the whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request, its younger records too, and reports it on "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers. Only the past side of the window needs a deadline: a retry arrives later, never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier, so it can’t carry a record further ahead of Matomo’s clock than it was. The window is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured with the device’s clock, which Matomo can’t see: a device whose clock is wrong by more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a day has every record refused, without an error. A clock that reads NaN or infinite has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every record left out and reported."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To keep older records, send them to a server you run, such as a TraffluentCollector, and have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that server forward them to Matomo with a token of a user who has write access to the site,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"added as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token_auth"},{"type":"text","text":" to its bulk request’s JSON. A token on a server stays secret. This module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t do that."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Visitors are sessions","anchor":"Visitors-are-sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo counts a visitor per ","type":"text"},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", 16 hexadecimal digits. The destination sends the last 64 bits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, in lowercase hex. Nothing else identifies a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record: no ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"cid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", device identifier or account. So Matomo’s visitors are sessions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its returning-visitor and visits-per-visitor reports say how long sessions last, not whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"people come back. That is the library’s default, for privacy. Each session is one visit as long","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the sessions enricher’s timeout is no longer than Matomo’s visit length, 30 minutes by default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"visit_standard_length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). With a longer timeout, a session that pauses for longer than Matomo’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visit length becomes two visits of one visitor.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record with no session, from a tracker without the sessions enricher, is its own visitor: its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the last 64 bits of the record’s identifier. A record a store recovered after a relaunch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its session, and with it the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Making up a session would join unrelated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records, and skipping the record would lose it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo recognizes a visitor by "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and, failing that, by a fingerprint of the request’s IP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"address, User-Agent, language and a daily salt, within 30 minutes. A new session’s first event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has an "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" Matomo hasn’t seen, so Matomo may fold it into another visit from the same address"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and User-Agent: an earlier session on the same device, or a session of another person behind the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same network. Set "},{"code":"trust_visitors_cookies = 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"code":"[Tracker]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in Matomo’s "},{"code":"config.ini.php","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have Matomo match a request that has an "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by its "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, for every site of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"installation. When Matomo’s privacy setting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to force tracking without cookies is on, Matomo ignores "},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and every visit is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingerprint’s."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo records the address each request comes from, as no app can override it without a token."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It masks part of the address before storing it when “Anonymize Visitors’ IP addresses” is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Administration, Privacy, Anonymize data). In Matomo 5.14 and 6.0 it is on, masking 2 bytes, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an installation whose administrator has never changed it, so a fresh install has it on, and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"older one keeps the setting it had. Matomo still uses the full address for geolocation and for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fingerprint above unless “Also use the Anonymized IP addresses when enriching visits” is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"too, which is off by default. Check both settings before you send."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Matomo receives","anchor":"What-Matomo-receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON object, ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"requests\":[…]}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", holding one tracking request per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first: ","type":"text"},{"code":"?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a query string, every value percent-encoded but for letters, digits, ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"code":"~","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each tracking request is a Matomo event:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Parameter","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"idsite","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The site ID","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rec"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiv"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session’s last 64 bits, or the record’s"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cdt"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s time, in whole seconds since 1970","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ca"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so Matomo doesn’t take the request for a page view should its Events plugin be off","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"e_c","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The category you give, such as your app’s name"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"e_a","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s name"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lang"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s locale, as a BCP 47 identifier, when it has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dimension<ID>"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The value of each property the dimensions map","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo’s Events reports group events by category, then action, then name. The category is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument you give, as an app’s events have no grouping Matomo would show better, and the action is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event’s name, so the Event Actions report lists your events. No event name (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_n"},{"text":") or value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_v"},{"text":") is sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The User-Agent is the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" sends, which Matomo reads for the device and operating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system. The rest of the standard context isn’t sent."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Custom dimensions","anchor":"Custom-dimensions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo numbers each site’s custom dimensions as you make them (Administration, Websites, Custom","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dimensions), so ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" maps your plan’s property names to their IDs:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"[\"plan\": 1, \"seats\": 2]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A property is mapped by name in every event that has it. Its value is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a string as it is, a number as JSON writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, a Boolean as ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and an array or object as its JSON. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends no value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property is never sent, whatever the record reveals, so it can’t be mapped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A property no dimension is mapped to is never sent, and the record goes without it. When the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination is made, it logs a notice for each event with such properties, once.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)"},{"text":" lists them, so a test can check that every property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you mean to send has a dimension.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws for a dimension ID below 1, a property mapped twice, a property no event of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan has, a property that is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" in an event, and two properties of one event mapped to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one dimension, checked in that order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make each dimension in Matomo with the Action scope, so each event keeps its own value. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension of the Visit scope holds one value a visit, the last one sent. Matomo ignores a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension it has no dimension of that ID for, and stores at most 250 characters of a value."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write, or that Matomo would refuse or change, is left out and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name is empty once Matomo removes line breaks and trims it, or longer than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"4,096 characters Matomo stores of an action;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose timestamp has no whole seconds of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64"},{"type":"text","text":", or is more than 23 hours from when the batch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is encoded;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a dimension’s value longer than 250 characters;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose tracking request is more than a request of 1,000,000 bytes can hold."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lengths are counted as Matomo stores the text: without line breaks or NUL characters, trimmed of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spaces and tabs at either end, and with "},{"code":"&","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":">","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"'","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" written as the HTML entities"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Matomo stores them as, so "},{"code":"&","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" counts 5. Matomo removes the line breaks and trims the spaces of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name or value it keeps too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event of the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose name would be left out."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What Matomo doesn’t report","anchor":"What-Matomo-doesnt-report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo answers 200 to a bulk request it can read, whatever its tracking requests hold. One it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses is counted as ","type":"text"},{"code":"invalid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the answer’s JSON and not stored, and only a request with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"token learns which. When the answer says Matomo refused every one, as for a site ID of no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"site, the destination drops the request and reports it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When it tracked some and refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"others, the refused ones are lost with only a notice in the log, as the answer doesn’t say which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they were. When its counts add up to fewer than the request’s tracking requests, or are both 0,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo skipped some without saying so, as after a database lock wait timeout, and the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends the request again until its deadline; Matomo counts the ones it had tracked twice.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A server with the QueuedTracking plugin’s queue turned on answers every bulk request with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"image as soon as it queues the request, before it checks any tracking request in it. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination counts the request as delivered. The server stores the valid tracking requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later, and it drops the rest, such as those for a site ID of no site, without reporting them. On","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such a server, check the site ID before you ship, and check that the first events show up in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"site’s Visits Log.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A server set to require a token for every bulk request (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bulk_requests_require_authentication"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refuses each one: Matomo 6.0 without the QueuedTracking queue answers 401, which the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drops and reports, and Matomo 5.14 answers 500, which the destination retries until the request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is cancelled. Leave that setting off.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Matomo stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch again, and when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and Matomo counts each copy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Matomo receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding"},"references":{"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding/MatomoDimensions/unmappedProperties(in:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unmappedProperties"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatomoEncoding0A16UnmappedPropertyV","text":"MatomoUnmappedProperty"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The properties of ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s events that no mapping names, and that Matomo is never sent.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/matomodimensions\/unmappedproperties(in:)","kind":"symbol","title":"unmappedProperties(in:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)"},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding/MatomoBatchEncoder/init(siteID:dimensions:category:plan:limit:now:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An encoder of the events "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" describes, for the Matomo site "},{"code":"siteID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sending each event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"code":"category","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and each property "},{"code":"dimensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps as its custom dimension, splitting each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to "},{"code":"limit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and leaving out the records tracked too long before, or after, the time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"now","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives."}],"url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/matomobatchencoder\/init(siteid:dimensions:category:plan:limit:now:)","title":"init(siteID:dimensions:category:plan:limit:now:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/init(siteID:dimensions:category:plan:limit:now:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"siteID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":":